<title>URUGUAY: Uruguay June inflation 1.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Uruguay June inflation 1.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MONTEVIDEO 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uruguayan consumer price inflation was 1.3 percent in June, compared to a 1.29 percent rise in prices in June last year and a 1.34 percent rise this May, the National Statistics Institute said Thursday.</p>
<p>Annual inflation was 21.1 percent in June, the lowest since December 1982. It compared to 28.19 percent annual inflation in June last year.</p>
<p>The most strongly rising prices in June were those of education and food.</p>
<p>((--Montevideo Newsroom +5982 92-0336))</p>
</text>
